## Method and reasoning
At each position choose an available value in sorted order and decrement its count. Restore the count when returning. There is one branch per distinct value, so copies never create duplicate branches. With P distinct permutations, the number of visited prefix states is at most 1+nP.

## Walk through the sample
For [2,1,2], choosing 1 first leaves a single continuation, 2,2. Choosing 2 first leaves the two continuations 1,2 and 2,1. Branching once per distinct available value yields exactly three lines.

## Complexity
Output takes O(nP), and the search stores O(n) state.

## Reference implementation
~~~
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

void generate(const vector<int> &keys, vector<int> &count, vector<int> &path, int n) {
    if (int(path.size()) == n) {
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)
            cout << path[i] << (i + 1 == n ? '\n' : ' ');
        return;
    }
    for (int i = 0; i < int(keys.size()); ++i)
        if (count[i]) {
            --count[i];
            path.push_back(keys[i]);
            generate(keys, count, path, n);
            path.pop_back();
            ++count[i];
        }
}
int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);
    int n;
    cin >> n;
    map<int, int> frequency;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
        int x;
        cin >> x;
        ++frequency[x];
    }
    vector<int> keys, count, path;
    for (auto [x, c] : frequency) {
        keys.push_back(x);
        count.push_back(c);
    }
    generate(keys, count, path, n);
}
